    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** (74.96) and **Josh Naylor** (72.21) anchor our lineup as the premier offensive threats. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to favorable park factors and a strong platoon alignment against Sonny Gray, while **Josh Naylor** exploits a hitter-friendly wind forecast and a favorable matchup against M. Keller. **Corbin Carroll** (71.26) also presents a high-floor opportunity; despite facing Leahy, his elite speed profile and the #3 spot in the order make him an essential play as we look to capitalize on his potential to swipe bags, our most scarcest category. **Brice Turang** (64.65) rounds out our top-tier options, bolstered by a significant boost for hitting out of the #2 spot, providing essential stability despite the difficult matchup against Lodolo.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who finished just outside the starting cut with a 47.35 score. While his stolen base upside is typically a major draw for Ghost Ride the WHIP, a harsh 13% penalty for an unfavorable platoon split against Mize ultimately forced him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency hitters. We are tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, specifically for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Max Muncy**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Travis Bazzana**; these projections rely on historical batting order data and are subject to immediate adjustment if managers shift the lineup. Notably, **James Wood** (53.36) remains a high-variance start; while his elite xwOBA of 0.404 and the #1 spot in the order offer massive potential, he is facing a tough individual matchup against Luzardo, and we must monitor if the high-efficiency expectations hold against such a disciplined arm. **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving no chance for a spot start today.",
